## Why This Is Asked

This question explores runtime extensibility, tenant isolation, and concurrency in a common caching scenario. It requires a concrete, runnable approach rather than a vague pattern description.

## Key Concepts

- **Strategy Pattern**: Enables pluggable eviction algorithms that can be swapped at runtime
- **Registry Pattern**: Manages policy factories for dynamic registration and lookup
- **Per-Tenant Isolation**: Each tenant gets its own policy instance to prevent cross-tenant contamination
- **Thread Safety**: Critical when multiple services access the cache concurrently

## Core Interfaces

```typescript
interface EvictionPolicy {
  onAccess(key: string): void;
  onInsert(key: string, value: unknown): void;
  evictIfNeeded(capacity: number): string[];
}

interface EvictionPolicyFactory {
  create(): EvictionPolicy;
}

class EvictionPolicyRegistry {
  private policies = new Map<string, EvictionPolicyFactory>();

  register(name: string, factory: EvictionPolicyFactory): void {
    this.policies.set(name, factory);
  }

  create(name: string): EvictionPolicy {
    const factory = this.policies.get(name);
    if (!factory) throw new Error(`Policy '${name}' not found`);
    return factory.create();
  }
}
```

## Usage Example: Custom TTL Policy

```typescript
class TTLEvictionPolicy implements EvictionPolicy {
  private accessOrder: string[] = [];
  private timestamps = new Map<string, number>();
  private ttlMs: number;

  constructor(ttlMs: number = 60000) {
    this.ttlMs = ttlMs;
  }

  onAccess(key: string): void {
    const idx = this.accessOrder.indexOf(key);
    if (idx > -1) this.accessOrder.splice(idx, 1);
    this.accessOrder.push(key);
    this.timestamps.set(key, Date.now());
  }

  onInsert(key: string, value: unknown): void {
    this.accessOrder.push(key);
    this.timestamps.set(key, Date.now());
  }

  evictIfNeeded(capacity: number): string[] {
    const now = Date.now();
    const evicted: string[] = [];

    while (this.accessOrder.length >= capacity) {
      const key = this.accessOrder.shift()!;
      const age = now - (this.timestamps.get(key) || now);

      if (age > this.ttlMs) {
        evicted.push(key);
        this.timestamps.delete(key);
      }
    }
    return evicted;
  }
}

// Register and use
const registry = new EvictionPolicyRegistry();
registry.register('ttl', () => new TTLEvictionPolicy(30000));

const tenantCache = {
  policy: registry.create('ttl'),
  data: new Map<string, unknown>()
};
```

## Thread Safety & Isolation

- **Per-Tenant Instances**: Each tenant cache holds its own policy instance, preventing interference
- **Synchronization**: Use `ReadWriteLock` or concurrent maps for multi-threaded access
- **Hot-Swapping**: Replace `tenantCache.policy` atomically when updating tenant config

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design runtime-extensible components using the Strategy pattern and a lightweight registry. Encourages thinking about a clean surface area, testability, and how policies interact with the core cache.

## Key Concepts

- EvictionPolicy interface: evictKey(store, capacity) and accessed(key) hooks
- EvictionRegistry: maps names to policy factories
- Cache core: get/put, fixed capacity, invokes policy to evict when needed
- Trade-offs: O(1) lookups, eviction latency, policy state maintenance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal eviction policy interface and implementations
class EvictionPolicy {
  accessed(key) { /* optional */ }
  evictKey(store, capacity) { throw new Error('not implemented') }
}

class LRUPolicy extends EvictionPolicy {
  constructor() { this.order = new Map(); }
  accessed(key) { if (this.order.has(key)) this.order.delete(key); this.order.set(key, true); }
  evictKey(store, capacity) {
    if (store.size <= capacity) return null;
    for (let k of this.order.keys()) {
      if (store.has(k)) return k;
    }
    return store.keys().next().value || null;
  }
}

class FIFOPolicy extends EvictionPolicy {
  constructor() { this.order = new Map(); }
  accessed(key) { /* FIFO does not update on access */ }
  evictKey(store, capacity) {
    if (store.size <= capacity) return null;
    for (let k of this.order.keys()) {
      if (store.has(k)) return k;
    }
    return store.keys().next().value || null;
  }
  registerInsert(key) { if (!this.order.has(key)) this.order.set(key, true); }
}

class EvictionRegistry {
  constructor() { this.factories = new Map(); }
  register(name, factory) { this.factories.set(name, factory); }
  create(name) { const f = this.factories.get(name); return f ? f() : null; }
}

class Cache {
  constructor(capacity, registry, policyName='lru') {
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.store = new Map();
    this.registry = registry;
    this.policy = registry.create(policyName) || new LRUPolicy();
  }
  setPolicy(name) { const p = this.registry.create(name); if (p) this.policy = p; }
  put(key, value) {
    this.store.set(key, value);
    if (this.policy && typeof this.policy.registerInsert === 'function') {
      this.policy.registerInsert(key);
    }
    while (this.store.size > this.capacity) {
      const k = this.policy.evictKey(this.store, this.capacity);
      if (k == null) break;
      this.store.delete(k);
    }
  }
  get(key) {
    if (!this.store.has(key)) return undefined;
    const v = this.store.get(key);
    if (typeof this.policy.accessed === 'function') this.policy.accessed(key);
    return v;
  }
}
```

